Z||000003||kornholio||10-24-1999||08:44 PM||||I don't know if this will be any help, but I get really crappy gas mileage with my automatic 86 V6 SE.  I average about 19 mpg just driving around town.  How can I improve this?  This is what I have replaced that supposedly helps:  EGR valve, EGR tube, EGR solenoid, spark plugs, wires, distributor cap & rotor, air filter, and fuel filter.  What else could be wasting my gas?  I wouldn't say that I have a lead foot, but I sure don't have a feather foot either!  I've heard of people getting 24-27 mpg with this engine.  Are they lying???||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||10-24-1999||10:43 PM||||My all time record city mileage with my formula 5-speed is 28mpg.  I drove like a little old lady and babied the thing.  I usually average 18-22 city, 32-34 highway. City depends on what kind of mood I'm in, highway depends on how many cops are out, the fewer cops I see, the lower my mpg <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 10-25-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||10-25-1999||03:43 PM||||87 4 cyl even with automatic should do better than that. If the TCC is not locking then you could get really crappy milage. when rolling down the highway, find a clear area and keep an eye on the tach while you tap the brakes. if the TCC is locked like it should be, then RPM will jump some when you tap the brake. tapping the brake will unlock the TC at any speed. It should lock, and drop the rpm as soon as you let off the brake pedal. you only need to push the brake pedal enough to activate the switch.<P>check the ECM for codes. If there is a code in the ECM it runs Open Loop, and that means it runs rich.||||reg||1
Z||000006||88formula||10-25-1999||07:49 PM||||Thase figures for gas mileage are really good for all those  V6's out there, even 19 miles to the gallon is pretty good for a V6. But what about you people out there who have four cyl automatics, what do you get? My TCC does work and there are no codes in the ECM. I checked the mileage again and came up with 20-MPG. this really sucks when a V6 gets the same or better than a four. One thing I did notice was that the car wants to stall when its really cold out first thing in the morning.There also seems to be more white smoke out the exhaust than normal. The car also emits a rotten egg smell all the time, what causes that to happen?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mark||10-25-1999||07:53 PM||||I've noticed a sharp decrease in the gas mileage on my '86 GT 4-speed.  However, there are no obvious indications of any problems.  The car runs great.  The plugs look fine (light grey).  Emission test results are very low.  Basic timing is right on the money. The only objectionable characteristics are strong exhaust odor upon deceleration and black exhaust tips.  Any suggestions?||||reg||1
Z||000008||kornholio||10-25-1999||09:12 PM||||I may be wrong, but I think I read somewhere that if you smell rotten egg from your exaust, your cat convertor is shot.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Standard||10-26-1999||12:49 AM||||I have an 84 4 banger and I usually get 20mpg in the city and 30 on the highway, but my engine's not quite tuned perfectly...<P>The rotten egg smell is comes from sulfur combining with hydrogen( i think, my mind just went blank) in the cat.  Can happen if the fuel in you area has lots of sulfur.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Formula||10-26-1999||04:42 PM||||If the cat or the muffler is going bad does it make a rattling noise at idle to 1500 RPM?<BR>And it sounds as though my exhaust has a pinhole leak in it. If I replace my cat with straight pipe will it affect performance at all? I've noticed the black tips too. And I get a smidgen of white smoke on start up. One last comment.......I would check for a rotten egg under the car someplace to if it smells really bad............I heard batboy say that if you pound the muffler in a certain place it stops making a rattling noise. Any comments? I'm kind of dissapointed because I just got my exhaust manifold leak fixed and everything else went wrong.||||reg||1
